BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BOOK LAUNCH - GOING SOUTH: TRACING THE MASAI FROM THE MIDDLE EAST 
 TO EAST AFRICA\, BY PAUL KUNONI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260808T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260808T190000
UID:bm-5960520260808@adifferentbooklist.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/1188585/PAUL_KUNO
 NI_BOOK_LAUNCH.png?cb=1785182783
DESCRIPTION:Join scientific researcher Paul Kunoni for the launch of his n
 ewly published book\, GOING SOUTH: TRACING THE MAASAI FROM THE MIDDLE EAST
  TO EAST AFRICA.\nWhat forces shaped the rise of the Maasai in East Africa
 \, and how did one family's story become intertwined with the region's com
 plex history of migration\, colonization\, and cultural survival?\n\nGoing
  South: Tracing the Maasai from the Middle East to East Africa by Paul Nku
 o Kunoni traces the historical\, cultural\, and political pathways that sh
 aped the Maasai people and their enduring legacy in the region.\n*GOING SO
 UTH will be available for purchase at the event.\nLook forward to remarks 
 from the author\, a live reading\, Q&A and an opportunity to have your cop
 y of the book signed by Paul.\nAdmission: Free. All are welcome! Students 
 and scholars especially of African history\, political science\, internati
 onal relations and the like\, will be interested in GOING SOUTH and Paul's
  talk. See you there!
LOCATION:Blackhurst Cultural Centre
URL:https://adifferentbooklist.com/events
X-SOURCE:A Different Booklist
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Book Launch: EAT WITH AFIA\, by Afia Amoako
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260818T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260818T203000
UID:bm-6017820260818@adifferentbooklist.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/1188585/Eat_With_
 Afia_Book_Launch.png?cb=1785773215
DESCRIPTION:Join us in celebrating Afia Amoako and the launch of her new b
 ook EAT WITH AFIA: A CELEBRATION OF PLANT-BASED GHANAIAN COOKING!\nAfia\, 
 a local food creator and public health researcher\, loves to cook and cele
 brate African food through culture\, history and tradition. At the launch 
 look forward to Afia sharing her story about her passion for African food 
 and about her book\, a Q&A\, and an opportunity to purchase the book and h
 ave it signed by her. Of course there will be refreshments inspired by the
  book\, so bring your appetite for stories and flavour!\n*Book is availabl
 e for pre-order now on our webstore and will be available on-site at the e
 vent.\nAdmission: Free.
LOCATION:Blackhurst Cultural Centre
URL:https://adifferentbooklist.com/events
